# Line endings are load-bearing, not cosmetic.
#
# Content hashes are computed over file bytes, and the governing records are embedded
# into the binary with `include_str!`. A clone with `core.autocrlf=true` would hand
# every one of them CRLF, changing every block hash and every bundle digest — so the
# same commit would validate on one machine and not on another.
#
# `nomos-spec-store` asserts this rather than trusting it: an embedded record carrying
# a carriage return fails a test.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.zip binary
*.docx binary
